what's going on guys this is rob and we  are back with another installment of our  beyond omega level series where we  discuss the most powerful characters in  comics and for this video we're stepping  into the marvel cosmic hierarchy and  talking about a character with one of  the weirdest names in all of comics the  in-betweener now the in-betweener was  created by jim starlin and first  appeared in warlock number nine in 1975  and the way marvel's pantheon of cosmic  beings works is that each of them are  basically the embodiment of some aspect  of the universe and in the case of the  in-betweener he's the embodiment of the  concept of duality now we're first  introduced to the in-betweener during an  altercation between adam warlock and his  evil counterpart the magus who had one  of the best afros in the history of  comics now magus summons the  in-betweener and states that he rules a  realm between fact and fantasy and that  his domain is the land between reality  and illusion now when the in-betweener  shows up he informs adam warlock that he  does the bidding of two other cosmic  entities master order and lord chaos  which as the names imply are the  embodiments of order and chaos within  the marvel universe the in-betweener  also states that he walks between all  concepts including life and death  reality and illusion good and evil logic  and emotion and god and man and claims  that he has the ability to affect all of  those concepts which suggests that he's  capable of manipulating reality itself  now the next time that we see the  in-betweener it's in the pages of doctor  strange which jim starlin was writing at  the time and we see that the universe is  being changed in some drastic ways by a  group called the creators who were  basically just using a device called the  cosmic wheel of change now doctor  strange teams up with a living star  named apollo and destroys the cosmic  wheel of change which sent the cycle of  change already happening in the universe  spiraling out of control and so the  creators take on human form and are  basically able to do anything they want  including transforming humans into  bistro forms and they create a version  of doctor strange that's half human half  wild boar called dr stranger yet which  is kind of weird and if it sounds like a  ridiculous concept yeah i mean that's  what marvel comics were in the 1970s  right it was just weird but regardless  all this changing of reality also  affects the ancient one who had  basically merged his consciousness with  the universe but found the changes  happening to reality so disorienting and  painful that he was forced to find a  physical form to inhabit and doctor  strange later finds him lying drunk in  an alley where the two of them were  attacked by four servants of the  creators and so after defeating them the  ancient one opens a portal and takes  doctor strange to the realm of power  that's beyond the creators which is  beyond a being or force like dormammu  but is a concept much like eternity the  entity of course turns out to be the  in-betweener who the ancient one  describes as all-powerful and a  separator of actualities now we learned  that the in-betweener was created by  master order and lord chaos to bring  about the balance between life and death  in the universe which is why he was  attempting to bring about the  transformation of adam warlock into the  magus and when that failed he sought to  use the creators to bring about the  balance he desired but doctor strange  messes that up when he broke the cosmic  wheel of change now it's revealed that  the in-betweener is nearly omnipotent  and also capable of interdimensional  teleportation as he effortlessly sends  doctor strange to another dimension now  when strange and the in-betweener engage  in battle the in-betweener is unaffected  by any of dr strange's spells and  repeatedly alters reality as he sends  strange from one dimension to another in  rapid succession all while proclaiming  that he's more powerful than eternity  himself now doctor strange is  temporarily driven insane by how badly  he's being bested by the in-betweener  and the only way he's able to gain a  victory here is by calling on the power  of the in-betweener's creators master  order and lord chaos now at this point  in history doctor strange was vastly  more powerful than he is now so the fact  that the in-betweener was just able to  wipe the floor with him with no  difficulty just shows how powerful this  guy is like quite literally doctor  strange had a magical spell for pretty  much anything he wanted to do now the  in-betweener then forges an alliance  with the elders of the universe a group  of extremely powerful entities such as  the collector and ego the living planet  all in an attempt to kill galactus now  the elders seek to destroy galactus  because they believe that doing so will  basically result in the balance between  death and eternity being disrupted which  would bring about the end of the  universe itself and so the elders  restore the in-betweener from the  mystical prison where he was imprisoned  by order and chaos and he sets off to  kill galactus now the battle between  galactus and the in betweener is  basically a stalemate until the elders  decide to help galactus using five of  the infinity stones and master order in  lord chaos once again imprison the  in-betweener but later as thanos began  his quest for the infinity gems he frees  the in-betweener from his prison as the  in-betweener had the soul stone embedded  in his forehead and so thanos of course  steals the stone and then leads the  in-betweener to deal with the  consequences of escaping chaos and  orders prison which presumably means  they end up punishing him in some way  anyway but during jonathan hickman's  time runs out storyline we saw the  in-betweener along with master order  lord chaos and all the rest of the  cosmic entities had all basically been  killed by the beyonders but after the  marvel universe is reformed he appears  once again this time in al ewing's  ultimates 2 series which was amazing in  this story we end up learning that  master order and lord chaos have  basically teamed up to kill the living  tribunal who's the personification of  law and judgment and seek to establish a  new hierarchy and so to achieve this  they decide to replace the living  tribunal and fill his role as the  personification of law themselves but to  do that they order the in-betweener to  be the catalyst for the two of them to  merge into one being called logos now  eventually logos is torn apart and  separates into its individual components  of master order lord chaos and the  in-betweener and this is really the last  time that we've seen him show up in the  marvel universe so yeah he's an  incredibly powerful character that's  nearly omnipotent he can basically do  anything he wants through his ability to  manipulate cosmic energy and alter  reality itself to achieve his desired  purpose of bringing about balance with  the only limit to his power being that  he is wholly subservient to master order  in lord chaos the in-betweener also  possesses an ability to discern the  exact energy that will be the polar  opposite of any opponent he's facing and  use it against them killing them  instantly he's also stated that he  believes himself to be the opposite of  galactus because his abilities don't  work on galactus which would explain why  neither of the two were able to gain a  meaningful advantage over the other  whenever it was that they fought so  having said that guys this is the  in-betweener this dude is op super  powerful but a lot of folks have been  asking for him so i figured we'd do them  if you guys want to see anybody else let  me know down in the comment section  thank you guys for watching and i will  catch you all later  peace
 

